From: Fanasina <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475: Add the EPSS L3 and the CPU bandwidth votes

sm8450.dtsi gives the cores no OPP table, so cpufreq-hw only scales the core
clock: the L3 cache, the LLCC and the DDR keep their idle floor under load.
Describe the EPSS L3 provider and give the three clusters an OPP table whose
opp-peak-kBps carries the LLCC, DDR and L3 votes of sm8550.dtsi (same cores,
same cpufreq-epss), taken by rank over the 16/20/21 frequencies of this SoC.
The DDR vote is capped at 3196000 kBps. Needs INTERCONNECT_QCOM_OSM_L3=y.

---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi | 398 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 398 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475.dtsi
@@ -317,3 +317,401 @@
 	capacity-dmips-mhz = <2386>;
 	dynamic-power-coefficient = <509>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * CPU DDR, LLCC and L3 bandwidth votes. sm8450.dtsi gives the cores no OPP
+ * table, so cpufreq-hw only sets the core clock and the L3 cache, the LLCC and
+ * the DDR stay at their idle floor under load. Describe the EPSS L3 provider
+ * and give each cluster an OPP table whose opp-peak-kBps carries the three
+ * votes (LLCC, DDR, L3) in the order of the "interconnects" paths, taken by
+ * rank from sm8550.dtsi (same CPU cores and cpufreq-epss). The DDR vote is
+ * capped at 3196000 kBps, the highest DDR level of this board. The epss_l3
+ * provider must be built in (INTERCONNECT_QCOM_OSM_L3=y), cpufreq-hw needs
+ * the path at probe. MASTER_EPSS_L3_APPS is 0 and SLAVE_EPSS_L3_SHARED is 1
+ * (dt-bindings/interconnect/qcom,osm-l3.h).
+ */
+&soc {
+	epss_l3: interconnect@17d90000 {
+		compatible = "qcom,sm8550-epss-l3", "qcom,epss-l3";
+		reg = <0 0x17d90000 0 0x1000>;
+
+		clocks = <&rpmhcc RPMH_CXO_CLK>, <&gcc GCC_GPLL0>;
+		clock-names = "xo", "alternate";
+
+		#interconnect-cells = <1>;
+	};
+};
+
